  "title": "Evolution of Resource Use Through Behavior Imitation",
  "description": "Adds cultural evolutionary dynamics through behavior imitation to the evolution of resource-use behavior. Simulates several imitation biases (majority, minority, most successful, most experienced, parents), showing how norms and traditions of sustainable or unsustainable resource use can emerge based on imitation bias, innovation rate, and agent mobility.",
